      en: "La Milpa is the third largest Maya city in Belize after Caracol and Lamanai. Its monumental architecture suggests it was a regional capital of the Rio Bravo region. The site includes a series of stelae depicting rulers in ceremonial attire. A causeway connects the main plaza to a smaller residential complex. The city's water system utilized reservoirs. The site is part of a nature reserve protecting endangered species.",
